  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></math>Methyl propyl bromide reacts with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>and&nbsp;gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8216;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo></math> whereas on reaction with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math> it gives&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8216;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo><mo>.</mo></math> The mechanism followed in these reactions and&nbsp;the products <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8216;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8216;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo></math> respectively are:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
